<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The hardened runtime's exceptions, for a signed build. The first is what
  Electron's V8 needs (JIT); the other two let macOS ask for the microphone
  (sound in) and the camera (the scene camera).

  Two that electron-builder's own template carries are left out on purpose
  (the security audit of 2026-10-28, finding 13), because each lets a program
  that is not ours run inside a process that holds the microphone and camera:
  `disable-library-validation` (any dylib may be loaded, signed or not, by
  anyone) and `allow-unsigned-executable-memory` (writable-and-executable
  pages without the JIT's own entitlement; V8 asks for JIT pages through
  `allow-jit` alone, as Chrome itself ships). If a signed build ever fails to
  start with a "code signature" or "library not loaded" line in Console, put
  `disable-library-validation` back first and say why here; the packed desktop check
  on the Mac (the one named in PLAN 23.17m) starts the app as it ships. (No double
  hyphens inside this comment: XML forbids them, and codesign stopped on one.)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
